WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.400
Tesla plans 16 new superchargers on a vacant Somerset site beside the A303 after a motorhome business closed. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 628. Tesla submitted plans for 16 supercharger stalls at the former Southfield's Enterprise Park site near Ilmanster. The application includes one disabled bay and a new substation on the eastern edge. Somerset Council should reach a decision within three months.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.600
The location sits at the park entrance close to coast to coffee and McDonald's.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.980
Planning potential noted the project uses a vacant site efficiently and aids long-distance

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:39.920
electric travel.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.140
The motor home business closed after 14 years in late July.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.860
Tesla filed the application just over two months later.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.900
The layout matches another proposed site at Windcanton Gateway further along the A303.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.300
A buffer zone stays at the western edge near the coast of coffee area.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:04.040
Elon Musk stated on X that Tesla and SpaceX will build and operate TerraFab.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:10.520
He emphasized zero doubt on ownership and said TSMC could only sublease part of the complex.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.560
The statement ended speculation that started after a report last week on TSMC exploring

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:17.720
operational roles.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.220
Intel stays involved in design, build, and packaging.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:27.020
The plant targets chips for Optimus, CyberCab, and SpaceX orbital data centers.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:32.860
Musk introduced TerraFab in March as a joint Tesla, SpaceX, and XAI effort.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.340
The aim is annual output supporting one terawatt of computing power.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.680
Intel joined the project in April.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:45.120
California's virtual power plant sent five gigawatt hours to the grid across ten events

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:45.700
this year.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.440
All energy came from customer power walls.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:54.520
The September 9 heatwave event alone produced 517 megawatts from Powerwalls.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.100
About 110,000 Powerwalls joined that dispatch.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:03.540
Five gigawatt hours could power roughly 1.2 million U.S. homes for a day.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.260
That September event represented about 1.55 gigawatt hours.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.620
It set a U.S. record for residential battery dispatch.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:19.100
A later October 6th event reached 601 MW from 85,774 Powerwalls.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.940
The dispatch delivered 932 MW hours.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.020
The prior single event peak stood at 517 MW.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.280
The program coordinates customer batteries for peak demand periods.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.300
Tesla will show the CyberCab and Optimus Gen 2 at the Paris Motor Show.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.200
The show runs October 12th through 18.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:45.500
Visitors can take supervised full self-driving test drives on-site, an owner-enabled track

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.920
mode with race and drift presets on a non-performance model-wide juniper.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.220
The feature functions across the lineup despite not being officially offered on base models.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.840
The owner called the omission a business decision rather than a technical barrier.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:06.540
Tesla extended new features to every cyber truck and every Model 3 or Y ordered on or after

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.660
October 1st.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.740
The update carries no extra cost for those buyers.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:16.820
President Trump will present Elon Musk with the National Medal of Science on October 8th.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:21.300
The medal ranks as the nation's top honor for scientific and technological achievement.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.540
Musk joins other recipients at the White House Summit.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.540
The award dates back to the Kennedy administration.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:34.200
Full self-driving version 14.3.11 showed strong U-turn performance during testing.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:39.760
owner's posted video of the maneuver on city streets. Space X set the cargo

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.480
dragon's CRS 35 launch for October 13th. The mission carries the final rollout

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.720
solar arrays for the International Space Station. Halloween mode will reach

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.400
the full self-driving software branch soon. Kalena Brown confirmed the update

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.120
arrives without any subscription change. The mode adds ghost-car visuals and

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:05.240
themed wraps. A cyber cab lost its entire left-door panel in a low-speed Philadelphia crash.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.300
The incident revealed the doors inner frame and internal parts. Owner video confirmed the same

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:18.320
details in a secret report. Tesla recorded 565 vehicle registrations in India from June through

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:25.040
September. That volume equals about 0.8% of the national market. It also represents roughly

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:31.380
30% of the premium segment. Showroom growth continues across the country. Dutch regulators

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.860
cleared a Europe-specific full-self-driving version. The software drops some US features,

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:43.160
but keeps a mode allowing speeds up to 50% above detected limits. European regulators raised

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:49.310
questions about Tesla's safety claims on the speed offset feature. The review focuses on how the

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:55.790
effects overall safety. Tesla holds 1.48 million active full-self driving subscriptions.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:03.090
The company runs Robotaxi Service in seven U.S. metro areas. UBS lifted its Tesla price target

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:11.530
to $391 from $385. The firm kept its buy rating and pointed to AI and autonomous driving upside.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:17.430
Cyber truck deliveries of the lower priced version have not raised overall volume to expected levels.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:21.950
Other Tesla models recorded sharper delivery drops in the same period.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.650
The company keeps adjusting pricing and incentives on the pickup.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.710
Sales stay below internal targets even after the price cut.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.590
The pickup continues facing challenges reaching wider adoption.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:39.190
Owning a semiconductor fabrication plant moves capital from variable supplier contracts

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.670
into fixed facility costs and long-term depreciation.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:48.630
Tesla and SpaceX chose to build and run TerraFab instead of depending on external foundries

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.490
for every wafer.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:55.230
This step secures access to process nodes while contract manufacturers juggle capacity

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.210
demands for many AI clients.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.230
The choice converts per wafer fees into upfront construction and equipment spending that stays

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.350
on the books for years.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.170
Utilization rates determine the economics.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:12.410
A dedicated line can maintain higher average loads than a shared fab balancing multiple

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:19.590
orders. Yet the dedicated line also demands ongoing equipment refreshes every 2-3 years. Intel

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:25.390
handles packaging while core front-end processes remain inside the Tesla Space X joint entity.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:32.110
The setup cuts allocation risks during shortages, but raises exposure to yield and ramp execution.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.650
Yield gains directly lower the cost per inference chip for Optimus and CyberCab.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:43.950
The decision shapes gross margin on autonomy hardware, meeting internal cost targets reduces

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:49.650
the bill of materials per computer, lagging yields increase per unit expense from the same

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.590
capital commitment.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:55.810
The real balance sits between supply certainty and manufacturing learning curve risk.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:02.170
Before we go, watch for the Paris Motor Show displays starting October 12th, and that's

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:13.590
wrap on today's Tesla news. TSLA closed at $377.81, down $2.87, or 0.8%.

